{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914844740},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me break down this task:\n1. I need to find the total number of farmers markets in the US from the first dataset\n2. I need to find the total US population from the census file\n3. I need to calculate: (total farmers markets / total population) * 100,000\n4. The answer should be to four decimal places and verified-by-construction\n\nFollowing the AGENTS.md instructions, I should:\n1. First check if there are semantic models in the catalog that might already have this data\n2. Then check for declared aliases\n3. If the data isn't already there, I need to ingest both CSV files as catalog entries\n4. Use xorq_select to get the values\n5. Use xorq_verify to verify the answers\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for existing data or semantic models."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01H75wK7JBx6tmi6w1MpyMPG","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01NxUisqX4AVNiVbjCZCySM2","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":332,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8157,"totalTokens":8499,"cost":{"input":0.00000